# GammaOS zram + block swap fstab for the RG DS Plus (microSD boot).
# Activated by init.rk30board.rc at boot-complete:
#   swapon_all /vendor/etc/fstab_swap.ext${vendor.ext_ram}
# with vendor.ext_ram=1024 and persist.sys.zram_enabled=1 (both in build.prop).
#
# One swap device: zram0, lz4-compressed RAM swap, disksize 1GB logical. comp_algorithm
# lz4 is set in init.rk356x.rc; the physical cap (zram0 mem_limit) and the writeback
# backing device are set in init.gammaos-io.rc, both before this swapon.
#
# The dedicated 2GB 'swap' partition (GPT label 'swap', /dev/block/by-name/swap) is NOT a
# second swap device any more: it is zram0's writeback backing device. As a lower-priority
# swap it was never used (the kernel only moves to the next device when zram runs out of
# slots, not when zram's RAM cap is hit), so once the cap was reached every swap-out failed
# and the system thrashed in place while 2GB of card swap sat empty. As the backing device
# it receives zram's incompressible pages (game data that lz4 cannot shrink, stored 1:1 in
# RAM otherwise) and its idle pages, pushed by the zram_writeback service.
#<src>                    <mnt_point>   <type>   <mnt_flags>   <fs_mgr_flags>
/dev/block/zram0          none          swap     defaults      zramsize=1073741824,swapprio=2
